Lab Material
Lab 20: End-to-End Integration with Camel Routes
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Build an Apache Camel integration route that reads CSV order files from a directory and parses them into Java objects
Enrich order data by querying a PostgreSQL database through Camel's JDBC component with a HikariCP connection pool
Apply Enterprise Integration Patterns (Content Enricher, Content-Based Router, Dead Letter Channel) within a single Camel route
Configure error handling with a dead letter channel and redelivery policy for failed messages
Verify the integration end to end by dropping a sample order file and inspecting generated output files and log output
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Java programming concepts and Maven project structure
Familiarity with SQL basics (SELECT, INSERT statements)
Experience with Linux command line operations
Basic knowledge of CSV data formats
Your practice environment should have the following installed. Verify each before continuing:

java -version
mvn -version
psql --version
If any are missing, install them with:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y openjdk-11-jdk maven postgresql postgresql-contrib
Lab Environment Setup
This lab uses an isolated, self-owned practice environment (a local Linux machine or VM). All components run locally: no external network calls or third-party services are contacted. This keeps the lab safe, repeatable, and fully offline-capable for defensive/educational integration training.

